    {
      "text": "\nWe need only those song where listen_date is equal to release data\nso......\n\nWhen you join  it's going to scan both the data set completely to avoid that\n\npartition pruning concept is used\n\n**How**\n\n\n1. first filter our data from spotify listening list  for which we are looking\n2. pass the same filter to larger data sets and scan only selective data (listen_date) in parititonedSpotifyListeningActivityDf\n\n",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/markdown",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "markdown",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "06fa950df9af458088343"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\ncustomerDF.write.format(\"parquet\").partitionBy(\"city\").mode(\"overwrite\").save(\"FileStore/tables/suankiData/processed/parititionCustomerData\")",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "4bd30d7cf2144e9ebc6b4"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\ncustomerPartitionedDf.filter(f.col(\"city\") === \"new_york\").count",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "b78bbbb0dbde4cd08b4b7"
    },
    {
      "text": "%spark\n\nval filterSongDf = spotifySongDf.selectExpr(\"song_id\", \"title\", \"artist_id\",\"to_date(release_date) as  release_date\").filter(col(\"release_date\") === \"2023-01-01\")\nval joinCond =  { parititonedSpotifyListeningActivityDf.col(\"listen_date\") === filterSongDf.col(\"release_date\")  &&\n                  parititonedSpotifyListeningActivityDf.col(\"song_id\")  === filterSongDf.col(\"song_id\") \n}\n\nval joinDF =parititonedSpotifyListeningActivityDf.join(filterSongDf, joinCond,\"inner\")",
      "config": {
        "colWidth": 12,
        "fontSize": 9,
        "enabled": true,
        "editorMode": "ace/mode/scala",
        "editorSetting": {
          "params": {},
          "forms": {},
          "language": "scala",
          "editOnDblClick": false,
          "completionKey": "TAB",
          "completionSupport": true
        }
      },
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      },
      "id": "d387d6f00ac64230af5c0"
    },
    {
      "text": "\n#problem statement\n 1. Analyse the listening activity of users:\n\n    - after 2019-12-31\n    - on the relase date of a song",
